  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Part double part single side extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey side extension,\r\nin conjunction with the proposed dormer, by reason of inappropriate design,\r\ncumulative excessive bulk and massing would result in an unduly obtrusive and\r\nincongruous addition that would poorly relate to the existing dwelling detracting\r\nfrom the character of the host property, the terrace in which it sits and\r\nproperties in the surrounding area. The development is contrary to the high\r\nquality design aspirations set out in The National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2024), policies D3 (D(1) and D(11)) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B on\r\nthe Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Local\r\nPlans Policies (2013) and Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;PT Sans, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of the site\r\nbeing located within an area of land liable to flooding and the lack of a\r\ncomprehensive Flood Risk Assessment, due to a lack of flood data, flood mitigation measures which\r\ntake into account the depth of the flood, and compensatory flood storage\r\ndetails, has failed to demonstrate that the proposed development would not\r\nexacerbate the risk of flooding within the site or increase the risk and\r\nconsequences of flooding elsewhere, contrary to the National Planning Policy\r\nFramework (2024), Policy SI12 and SI13 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.U\r\nof Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and Policies DM9 and DM10 of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;font face=&quot;PT Sans, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Due\r\nto its siting, proximity to the boundaries, bulk, scale, height and massing,\r\nthe proposed two storey side extension and rear dormer would result in undue overbearing and visual impacts to the gardens of Nos. 80\r\nand 82 Cecil Road, to the detriment of the amenities of those neighbouring occupiers.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal is contrary to the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework (2024), Policies D3.D(7) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1\r\nof the Harrow Core Strategy (2013), policy DM1 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument: Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
